  "insights": [
   "Novartis reported negative Phase 3 HARBOR trial data for del-desiran in myotonic dystrophy type 1 (DM1), failing the primary endpoint of video hand opening time (vHOT) versus placebo.",
   "Del-desiran was a key asset from the $12bn Avidity acquisition, modeled by Goldman Sachs as a $3.3bn opportunity at 50% probability of success.",
   "The failure adds significant risk to Novartis's post-2030 growth outlook, as del-desiran and pelacarsen were expected to help offset $25bn in patent losses (LoEs) during 2030-32.",
   "Goldman Sachs expects a mid-single-digit negative share price reaction, noting the stock is currently trading near all-time highs with the highest multiple in the sector.",
   "While Novartis reiterated its 2025-30 sales CAGR of 5-6%, the report highlights the lack of reiteration for post-2030 ambitions and questions the company's external innovation strategy.",
   "Other Avidity-acquired assets remain on track, with del-zota filed for accelerated approval and del-brax planning FDA meetings following positive Phase I/II biomarker data.",
   "Novartis's YTD performance (+14% vs SXDP -1.6%) is expected to unwind as earnings momentum has stalled and key pipeline readouts have failed."
